          "target:target:hun:79727724b5fa300482132d51"
        ],
        "explanation": "The old message ended with a stray '>' after \"value(s).\". The new line replaces \"value(s)\" with a choice format but ends with \"values}.<\". The file has no trailing newline, so the final '<' is part of the message value. The message therefore ends with \".\" followed by a literal '<'. The change swapped one stray character for another instead of removing it.",
